[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1069","stub":{"id":"1069","section":"2. Route 1567 below Duke Dam to US Route 501","altname":"","river":"Eno","difficulty":"ItoIII","states":["USA-NCR"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"2.17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:05:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112197","location":{"latitude":"36.0462989807129","longitude":"-79.0110015869141"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117479","location":{"latitude":"36.0717010498047","longitude":"-78.9089965820312"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101250388","title":null,"post_date":"2013-07-02 04:00:00+00","detail":"Saturated ground and some higher than normal flows over the last few weeks have added numerous new trees/strainers into the river. Use caution. Guess Rd Dam (Duke Dam), and just above Sennett's Hole both have large new trees crossing more than half the river. There are routes around them but they should be scouted.","user":{"name":"Banks Dixon"}}],"photos":[{"id":"874293","ext":"png","post_id":"874294","description":"This is a screenshot from some video I shot at Geer Dam.  The level was somewhere around 5.3 and there is a sweet V wave that forms off the corner of the dam where it was broken.","caption":"Reed's Loop","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/874293","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/874293"}},{"id":"873287","ext":"dv","post_id":"873288","description":"This little hole is located just below the Guess Rd bridge around 5.4 on the AW gauge.","caption":"Eno Fun","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/873287","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/873287"}},{"id":"882959","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885640","description":"Santa was spotted having a little fun before the big night!","caption":"Santa Park n' Play","poi_name":"Guess Rd Dam Wave","subject":"Santa","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882959","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882959"}},{"id":"882961","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885642","description":"","caption":"Santa Park n' Play","poi_name":"Guess Rd Dam Wave","subject":"Santa","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882961","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882961"}},{"id":"872743","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872744","description":"This is the ledge hole below Guess Rd on the Eno.  The level here was 3.14 on Rt.1516 - 501.\r\nGreat spot for spinning, low angle ends at this level.","caption":"Eno Bredge at Guess Rd","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872743","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872743"}},{"id":"873242","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"873243","description":"","caption":"Guess Rd \"Bredge\"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/873242","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/873242"}},{"id":"882136","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"884819","description":"","caption":"Canoeing Guess Dam","poi_name":"Guess Dam (Duke Dam)","subject":"","author":"B. Dixon","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882136","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882136"}},{"id":"6593","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6779","description":"This is the old Guess-Geer Dam, close to the Guess Road Bridge. The right side of the dam is blasted away. ","caption":"Guess Geer dam","poi_name":"Guess-Geer Mill Dam","subject":"Sandra Kofler","author":"Richard Kofler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6593","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6593"}},{"id":"6596","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6779","description":"This is a trouble spot for many novice canoers. At 4 feet is class 2+, but get quickly to a 3+ at higher levels","caption":"Running the Guess-Geer dam","poi_name":"Guess-Geer Dam","subject":"Sandra Kofler","author":"Richard Kofler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6596","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6596"}},{"id":"6597","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6779","description":"This is the old Guess-Geer dam, close to the Guess Road Bridge. The right side of the dam is blasted away. \r\n\r\nScouting is recommended at any level.","caption":"Guess Geer dam","poi_name":"Guess Geer dam","subject":"Sandra Kofler","author":"Richard Kofler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6597","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6597"}},{"id":"882958","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885639","description":"","caption":"Santa Park n' Play","poi_name":"Guess Rd Dam Wave","subject":"Santa","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882958","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882958"}},{"id":"882960","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885641","description":"","caption":"Santa Park n' Play","poi_name":"Guess Rd Dam Wave","subject":"Santa","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882960","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882960"}},{"id":"874295","ext":"png","post_id":"874296","description":"This is a screenshot from some video I shot at Geer Dam on the Eno.  A sweet V wave forms at certain levels off the corner of the dam where it was broken.  Great spot for lefty blunts!  The level was around 5.3 on the AW site.","caption":"Mike's Lefty Blunt","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/874295","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/874295"}},{"id":"6594","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6779","description":"There are many, nice rapids between the Colemill Park and WestPoint. At 4.0 on the USGS gage, the river is a class 2+, at 6 feet it gets pushy, at 8 feet, it's similar to the Ocoee  ","caption":"One of the many, smaller rapids","poi_name":"One of the many, small rapids between Colemill and Westpoint","subject":"Sandra Kofler","author":"Richard Kofler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6594","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6594"}},{"id":"6595","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6780","description":"This is a beautiful rock garden, approx 1 mile downriver of the Pleasant Green put in. It is easy at low water, above 6 feet it get's a little bit tricky.","caption":"Rockgarden, close to Pleasant Green","poi_name":"Not sure what the offical name is, we call it the Rockgarden","subject":"Rockgarden","author":"Richard Kofler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6595","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6595"}}],"detail":{"id":"1069","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This reach of the Eno River can be broken up into two sections:\n\nPleasant Green Canoe Access to Cole Mill Road\n(Section 3 in \"Paddling Eastern North Carolina\")\n\nCole Mill Road to West on the Eno City Park.\n(Section 4 in \"Paddling Eastern North Carolina\")\n\nThe entire reach is protected by [Eno River State Park](http://www.ils.unc.edu/parkproject/\nvisit/enri/home.html) and West Point on the Eno City\nPark. Both sections can be run in one day.\n\nTime estimates at about 4' on USGS:\n\nPleasant Green Rd to Cole Mill Rd is about 1.5 hours\n\nCole Mill Rd to Guess Rd is about 1 hour\n\nGuess Rd to West Point on the Eno(US501) is about half an hour\n\n### Put-in Directions:\n\nTo Pleasant Green Canoe Access:\n\nFrom Durham I-85 south to Highway 70 west(exit 170), turn right on Pleasant\nGreen Road, turn left into Canoe Access area just before crossing the river.\n\nTo Cole Mill Canoe Access:\n\nFrom Durham I-85 south to Cole Mill Road(exit 173), north on Cole Mill Road,\nleft on to Old Cole Mill Road, access is at end of road.\n\n### Shuttle Directions:\n\nPleasant Green Canoe Access to West Point on the Eno City Park:\n\nTake left out of canoe access parking lot onto Pleasant Green Road, right onto\nCole Mill Road. Turn left onto Umstead Road. Turn right onto Guess Road. Go\na short distance and turn left onto Latta Road. Turn right onto US501(Roxboro\nRoad). Cross river and turn right into West Point on the Eno City Park.\nFollow road to parking area close to the old mill.\n\nPleasant Green Canoe Access to Cole Mill Road Canoe Access:\n\nTake left out of canoe access parking lot onto Pleasant Green Road, right onto\nCole Mill Road. Turn right (at Umstead Road) onto Old Cole Mill Road, access\nis at end of road.\n\n### Guidebooks:\n\n[![](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/resources/repository/\\\nguide_east_nc.jpg)\\\n\\\nPaddling Eastern North Carolina](http://www.paddlingeasternnc.com)","averageGradient":"13","maxGradient":null,"length":"8.7","correlations":[{"reachID":"1069","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"2.2","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"7.1"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"ENO RIVER NEAR DURHAM, NC","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02085070","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"19","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:05:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:05:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.0722222","longitude":"-78.9077778"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/02085070","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02085070/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"2.17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:05:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112197","117479"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-79.01082949,36.04630715],[-79.01080119,36.04571081],[-79.01057899,36.04426881],[-79.01066132,36.04236681],[-79.01046779,36.04219588],[-79.01007939,36.04192561],[-79.00930259,36.04192561],[-79.00908059,36.04201581],[-79.00819292,36.04264668],[-79.00769359,36.04363808],[-79.00702779,36.04426901],[-79.00602912,36.04476481],[-79.00552972,36.04485488],[-79.00524179,36.04490381],[-79.00470599,36.04501261],[-79.00434879,36.04507908],[-79